.TH TIME-RANGER 1 "October 2026" "time-ranger 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
time-ranger \- distributed screen time aggregator for LAN
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B time-ranger
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B time-ranger
is a Go daemon that monitors screen time for users in a Unix group,
gossips state across LAN peers via mDNS and HTTP, and serves a real-time
dashboard on a configurable port.
.PP
All configuration is done through environment variables (see
.B ENVIRONMENT
below); the daemon takes no command line arguments.
.PP
At startup the daemon creates its data directory if needed (default:
the current directory) and starts collecting screen time information for
the monitored group, querying the
.B timekpra
CLI provided by
.BR timekpr-next (1).
.PP
It then serves:
.TP
.B Dashboard
A web UI with per-user and per-node statistics, listening on the loopback
interface only (default port 4848), and its JSON API:
.RS
.IP \fB/api/summary\fR
Aggregated today's totals per user.
.IP \fB/api/user?name=\fIuser\fR
Detailed screen time for a single user over the last week.
.RE
.TP
.B Peer gossip
An mTLS-protected HTTP endpoint used for anti-entropy synchronization with
other nodes on the LAN.  This is disabled unless a CA is configured (see
.BR TIME_RANGER_CA
below).  When enabled, peers are discovered via mDNS on
.IR _time-ranger._tcp .
.PP
The daemon reacts to
.B SIGTERM
and
.B SIGINT
and shuts down gracefully.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TIME_RANGER_GROUP
Unix group to monitor.  If empty, the first ten seemingly non-system
users from
.BR getent (1)
are used.
.TP
.B TIME_RANGER_UI_PORT
TCP port for the dashboard (default 4848, bound to localhost only).
.TP
.B TIME_RANGER_PEER_PORT
TCP port for peer communication/gossip (default 4849).  Publicly
accessible and protected with mTLS; only effective when
.B TIME_RANGER_CA
is set.
.TP
.B TIME_RANGER_CA
Path(s) to CA cert/key PEM file(s), comma separated.  When set, the peer
port is enabled with mutual TLS and gossip between nodes is used.
.TP
.B TIME_RANGER_DATA
Directory used to store persistent screen time data (default: the
current directory).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I %DATA%
Daily flat files recording screen time for each monitored user.  The data
directory is controlled by
.BR TIME_RANGER_DATA
above (for the packaged service it is
.IR /var/lib/time-ranger ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR timekpr-next (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR getent (1)
.PP
The dashboard can be opened at
.IR http://localhost:4848 .
